rsz: skip the per-endpoint progress row when the visit spent no pass

Per-pass cost fix from the repair-knobs campaign (ideas/repair-knobs-nihl.md,
third study). Not upstreamed; carried while it is measured. Changes no
result and no row that carries information.

With -verbose the setup sweep prints a progress row after every endpoint
it visits. On a design that closes, most visits find the endpoint already
repaired by earlier work and spend no pass: ibex cts visits 676 endpoints
for 104 passes and prints 676 rows, each repeating the previous one down
to the iteration number. After OpenROAD #11387 a row still collects the
TNS, the WNS and the worst pin and formats the line; the per-visit trace
of the default (patches/0078) puts the rows at 5-17% of the setup phase.

A per-endpoint row is printed only when the visit advanced the iteration
count. The ten-pass rows, the first and the final row are untouched.
diff --git a/src/rsz/src/policy/SetupLastGaspPolicy.cc b/src/rsz/src/policy/SetupLastGaspPolicy.cc
index 7e9fbfc00b..32f2a59d7e 100644
--- a/src/rsz/src/policy/SetupLastGaspPolicy.cc
+++ b/src/rsz/src/policy/SetupLastGaspPolicy.cc
@@ -367,9 +367,12 @@ void SetupLastGaspPolicy::runLastGaspLoop(
       break;
     }
 
+    const int iteration_before = last_gasp_state.opto_iteration;
     repairLastGaspEndpoint(endpoint_state, last_gasp_state);
 
-    if (config_.verbose || last_gasp_state.opto_iteration == 1) {
+    // As in the main phase: no row for a visit that spent no pass.
+    if ((config_.verbose && last_gasp_state.opto_iteration != iteration_before)
+        || last_gasp_state.opto_iteration == 1) {
       printProgress(
           last_gasp_state.opto_iteration, true, last_gasp_state.phase_marker);
     }
